  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling HIV Interventions among Key Affected Populations in Afghanistan - Afghanistan (01-Jan-2021-30-Sep-2021)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan, HIV, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Afghanistan)This program has the following goals: The goal of the NSP IV is to halt new HIV, STI &amp; Hepatitis infections and improve the health and quality of life of people living with and affected by HIV, STIs, and Hepatitis in Afghanistan over the next five years.. The objectives of this program are: To focus strategically on prevention services for HIV and other infections for key populations (PWID, MHRB, WHRB and prisoners).  To increase the coverage and quality of opiod substitution therapy for people who inject drugs by 2023.  To increase the coverage and quality of antiretroviral therapy services for people living with HIV by 2023.  To strengthen capacity and systems to generate strategic information on HIV, STIs and Hepatitis through biological and behavior surveillance, surveys and research for evidence-based response to the HIV, STIs and Hepatitis epidemic.  To improve the enabling environment to address enhanced coordination, human rights, positive legal environment, strengthened community systems, increased domestic funding, reduced stigma and discrimination, to address the needs and rights of key populations affected by HIV, STIs and Hepatitis</narrative>
  </description>
